  "notes": "Eventim Israel (Akamai-fronted). Plain clients are tarpitted (ReadTimeout — the auto-jsonld row's error, identical from the Mac, so NOT a geo wall): Chrome TLS impersonation is mandatory (fetch.impersonate; the 403/429 auto-switch never fires on a timeout). Akamai also 403s bursts and the all-Israel /events/ listings, and only PAGE 1 of a listing carries the schema.org ItemList of MusicEvents (?page=N pages have none), so the recipe reads page 1 of many narrow listings — 5 small city roots (≤25 events each) + 7 big cities × 7 categories — at a 4.5 s pace (54 requests, ~4.5 min). The artist sub-categories (1046/1047) and the big-city root pages were dropped: they duplicate the concerts page almost 1:1, and JSON-LD ids are seeded with the listing URL so overlap = duplicate rows. City/category ids come from the site's own URLs (slugs are ignored by the server). JSON-LD gives name, startDate, venue + Hebrew city (city_aliases), AggregateOffer lowPrice/ILS (0.0 = placeholder) and the /event/<id>/ purchase URL. The public-api.eventim.com exploration API would be cleaner but its robots.txt disallows everyone except Googlebot. Coverage ≈ the top ~24 per listing (TLV: 51 of 59); ~100 events in small towns without a city id stay out."
